Correct the range in the error for a bad input base. ibase may be up
to 36, as BC_NUM_MAX_IBASE says and as the testsuite checks, with A
to Z as digits, but the message for a value out of range still said
"must be [2,16]".

---
 miscutils/bc.c |    2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/miscutils/bc.c
+++ b/miscutils/bc.c
@@ -6016,7 +6016,7 @@
 
 	if (ib || sc || left->t == XC_RESULT_OBASE) {
 		static const char *const msg[] ALIGN_PTR = {
-			"bad ibase; must be [2,16]",                 //XC_RESULT_IBASE
+			"bad ibase; must be [2,36]",                 //XC_RESULT_IBASE
 			"bad obase; must be [2,"BC_MAX_OBASE_STR"]", //XC_RESULT_OBASE
 			"bad scale; must be [0,"BC_MAX_SCALE_STR"]", //XC_RESULT_SCALE
 		};
